---
// Help for ViewSwitcher for Mac, iPhone and iPad, also the App Store's support URL (SITE-17).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { github, site } from "../site.config";
const store = site.ipadApp.state === "store";
---
<Base title="Support for ViewSwitcher for Mac, iPhone and iPad" description="Help with ViewSwitcher for Mac, iPhone and iPad: getting set up with OBS, fixing common problems, and how to reach us." path="/support">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lede">Help with ViewSwitcher for Mac, iPhone and iPad. If your question isn't answered here, <a href={`${github}/issues/new`}>ask us on GitHub</a>. We read every one.</p>

    <h2>Getting set up</h2>
    <p>The short version is below. The full guide, with screenshots and a first stream: <a href="/setup">how to set up OBS with ViewSwitcher</a>.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Install <a href="https://obsproject.com">OBS</a>, the free streaming app, if you don't have it.</li>
      <li>In OBS, open <strong>Tools → WebSocket Server Settings</strong> and turn the server on. This is how ViewSwitcher talks to OBS.</li>
      <li>Open ViewSwitcher and press <strong>Set up OBS</strong>. It makes a "ViewSwitcher" scene in OBS and puts your views in it.</li>
      <li>In that scene, add your camera as a source named exactly <strong>Camera</strong>, and your screen as <strong>Screen</strong>. ViewSwitcher lists any it's still missing.</li>
      <li>Press <strong>Set up OBS again</strong>, and you're ready: pick a view and it goes on air.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Common problems</h2>
    <h3>ViewSwitcher says OBS isn't connected</h3>
    <p>Make sure OBS is open and its WebSocket server is on (Tools → WebSocket Server Settings).</p>
    <h3>The view is blank in OBS</h3>
    <p>In OBS, open Settings → Advanced and turn off <strong>Enable Browser Source Hardware Acceleration</strong>, then restart OBS.</p>
    <h3>My camera or screen doesn't show up in the view</h3>
    <p>Check that the source in the "ViewSwitcher" scene is named exactly <strong>Camera</strong> or <strong>Screen</strong>, then press Set up OBS again.</p>
    <h3>The iPhone or iPad app won't connect</h3>
    <p>Keep ViewSwitcher open on the Mac and plug the iPhone or iPad in with its cable. The first time, tap <strong>Trust</strong> when it asks about this computer. Without the cable, pair it over Wi-Fi (below). More in <a href="/ipad">ViewSwitcher for iPhone and iPad</a>.</p>
    <h3>Pairing over Wi-Fi</h3>
    <p>In ViewSwitcher's menu bar, turn on <strong>Let Phones and Tablets on This Wi-Fi Connect</strong>. In the iPhone or iPad app, tap <strong>Scan the code</strong> and point it at the QR code, or tap <strong>Enter code</strong> and type the code the Mac shows. Scan from the app, not the Camera app, which would pair Safari instead. In a phone's browser without the app, scan the QR code with the camera (or open the address under it and enter the code). Only devices you pair can switch scenes, and you can remove one any time. The phone and the Mac need to be on the same Wi-Fi; use it on networks you trust, like home or church Wi-Fi.</p>
    <p>If it can't find your Mac: check that the Mac isn't on a guest network that keeps devices apart, and that ViewSwitcher is allowed in <strong>Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Local Network</strong> on the iPhone or iPad. If Scan the code shows no camera, allow it in <strong>Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Camera</strong>.</p>

    <h2>Buying the iPhone and iPad app</h2>
    <p>ViewSwitcher for iPhone and iPad {store ? "is" : "will be"} a one-time purchase on the App Store, with nothing to subscribe to, and one purchase covers both. To install it on another iPhone or iPad, sign in with the same Apple Account and download it again from the App Store at no charge. For a refund, ask Apple at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</p>
    <p>ViewSwitcher for Mac is free.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, bugs and ideas: <a href={`${github}/issues`}>GitHub issues</a>. Please say which app you're using (Mac, iPhone or iPad) and what you expected to happen.</p>
    <p>How we handle your data: <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>.</p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
